###
### RIL / Telephony
###
# mtkfusionrild is MediaTek's rild. AOSP 10 has no hal_telephony_default_exec --
# hal_telephony is only an attribute (public/hal_telephony.te); the concrete
# exec type is rild_exec, which vendor/file_contexts uses for /vendor/bin/hw/rild.
# The binary itself lives in /vendor/bin/hw/ (rild.rc:1, proprietary-files.txt)
# and is started through ctl.start ril-daemon-mtk by the telephony stack.
/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/mtkfusionrild                                                  u:object_r:rild_exec:s0
# vtservice_hidl (init.vtservice.rc) is MTK's VoLTE video-telephony service;
# class hal, so it starts on class_start hal. /system/bin/vtservice is the
# companion service (class main) in its own domain: it is executed off
# /system, so sepolicy_tests requires the type to carry system_file_type
# and treble_sepolicy_tests requires the domain to carry coredomain.
/(vendor|system/vendor)/bin/hw/vtservice_hidl                                                 u:object_r:mtk_vtservice_exec:s0
/system/bin/vtservice                                                            u:object_r:mtk_vtservice_main_exec:s0
